# Amiga UI — Goose Project Hints

This repository builds a Python compatibility layer for selected classic Amiga
Workbench GUI applications, run under an in-process `vamos` launcher. The
first real target is `iTidy`.

This file is loaded automatically for every Goose session (interactive or
`goose run`). Keep it short; the substance lives in the docs below.

## Read First

- `AGENTS.md` — core repository rules (dependency management via `uv`, the
  `vamos` launcher as the standard execution path, subclass-over-monkeypatch,
  scope boundaries). Its line pointing to `openhands-onboarding.md` is for the
  OpenHands harness only — skip it.
- `docs/README.md` — documentation index. Run the triage helper before
  reading docs in full:
  ```bash
  uv run python tools/docs_triage.py
  uv run python tools/docs_triage.py --section runtime
  ```
- `.goose/README.md` — how to invoke the autonomous development recipe with
  `goose run`, and what its completion gate checks.

## Working Loop

Follow `docs/workflows/error-driven-porting.md`: run a real app under
`vamos`, capture the first meaningful failure, implement the smallest fix,
rerun. Follow `docs/workflows/branching-and-merging.md` for branch and merge
rules. Both docs describe their stop-marker mechanics in OpenHands terms —
for Goose, use `tools/goose_allow_stop.sh` instead (see `.goose/README.md`).

## Goose/Ornith Tool Discipline

Use only tools that Goose actually exposes in the current session. Do not copy
OpenHands-specific tool names such as `terminal` or `file_editor`, and do not
invent standalone `shell`, `find`, or `search` tools. Treat `find`, `rg`,
`grep`, `git grep`, `sed`, `cat`, and `ls` as shell commands to run through the
available Goose command/shell tool. If a tool call fails because the tool does
not exist or the arguments are invalid, change tools or arguments immediately
instead of repeating the same call.

## Canonical Commands

```bash
uv run amiga-ui check
uv run amiga-ui smoke-gui
uv run amiga-ui smoke-gui --direct
uv run amiga-ui probe amiga_apps/itidy1classic/binary/extracted/iTidy
uv run amiga-ui-xvfb -- <command> [args...]
uv run ruff check .
uv run pyright
uv run python -m unittest
uv run python tests/run_gui_smoke_test.py
```

## Optional Skills

`.agents/skills/` holds on-demand guidance for launcher work, host GUI
implementation, scope/boundary triage, code style, committing, assets, and
the error-driven porting loop. Read the relevant skill file when a task
matches its topic.
